proposed_comments.body:
`IndexOf` searches the localized sentinel entries and compares case-sensitively, while app names are user-controlled. If an app name differs only by case, or collides with a localized sentinel label such as "All apps" or "Global only", the filter can restore to the wrong option after a refresh. Search only the real app entries and use the same ordinal-ignore-case comparison as the rest of the filter.

**Severity:** `medium`

```suggestion
                int found = -1;
                for (int i = 2; i < AppFilterOptions.Count; i++)
                {
                    if (string.Equals(AppFilterOptions[i], previous, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                    {
                        found = i;
                        break;
                    }
                }
```

